# AI BlogNest API - Demo Video Script

## Introduction

Hello, this is my AI BlogNest API project.

AI BlogNest is a backend application designed to create,
manage, update, and delete blog posts through REST APIs.

The project uses Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB and Mongoose.

## Step 1 - Project Structure

First, I will show the project structure.

The project contains:

- config
- controllers
- models
- routes
- services
- server.js
- package.json
- .env

The application follows a modular MVC-style backend structure.

## Step 2 - Start the Server

I will open the terminal and start the application using:

npm run dev

The server starts on port 5000.

The API can be accessed at:

http://localhost:5000

## Step 3 - Test API

Now I will test the API using Postman.

First, I send a GET request:

GET /api/blogs

This returns the available blog posts.

## Step 4 - Generate AI Blog

Next, I demonstrate the AI blog generation endpoint.

I send a POST request:

POST /api/blogs/generate

Request body:

{
  "topic": "Artificial Intelligence"
}

The API processes the topic and returns a generated blog
with a title, content and tags.

## Step 5 - View Blog

Next, I use:

GET /api/blogs/:id

This retrieves a specific blog using its ID.

## Step 6 - Update Blog

I can update an existing blog using:

PUT /api/blogs/:id

For example, I can change the title or content.

## Step 7 - Delete Blog

Finally, I demonstrate:

DELETE /api/blogs/:id

This removes the selected blog from the database.

## Step 8 - Database

The application uses MongoDB to store blog information.

The main entities are:

User
Blog
Comment
Tag
BlogTag

The ER diagram shows the relationships between these entities.

## Conclusion

This completes the demonstration of my AI BlogNest API.

The project provides REST APIs for creating, reading,
updating and deleting blog content, with an AI-based
blog generation service.

Thank you.

